Z||000008||Bazooka||11-07-2001||07:59 PM||||Ali,<BR>  The AMX never came with a 396 engine. The 68-70 AMX had a 290, 343 or a 390 and the 71-74 AMX came with a 360 V8's.<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.members.aol.com:/m34chev/AMX.jpg">       <P>*********************************<BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ali_Gulf_Fiero:<BR>Wow, that takes me back 10 years. I had a Daytona. The stripped down CS with the Turbo II engine. That car SCREWED! I beat a hopped-up AMX a friend owned, and his other car - a Javelin.<BR>I made sure to race the AMX on a business park entrance road. Ingress and Egress sides diveded by a grassy median. I kicked that 396's A$$. When we dragged later on on a straight, he creamed me. Wah!<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>*********************************<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Bazooka (edited 11-07-2001).]||||reg||1
